    <section id="exp_40" class="exp-section">
        <div class="exp-header">
            <h2>EXPERIMENT 40: CLEAN PRODUCT CATALOG E-COMMERCE STORE</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>1. PROBLEM STATEMENT (QUESTION)</h4>
            <div class="question-box">39. user visits an online store that features a clean and straightforward product catalog, allowing 

them to easily browse and purchase items. The homepage displays a selection of featured products 

along with categories for quick navigation. Each product listing includes a clear image, description, 

price, and available options such as size or color. Users can add items to their shopping cart with a 

single click and view their cart at any time to adjust quantities or remove items. The website also 

includes a search bar for finding specific products and a filter option to refine results by price, 

brand, or popularity. Once the user is ready to check out, they can proceed to a secure checkout 

page where they enter shipping and payment details. The website also provides an order summary 

and confirmation, with the option to track their order status through their account.

1.Homepage:

• Design a visually appealing homepage that introduces the online store and showcases featured 

products.

• Include a search bar, navigation menu, and clear calls to action to encourage users to explore the 

product catalog.

2.Product Listings:

• Create individual pages for each product, complete with product descriptions, images, pricing, and 

availability status.

• Organize products into categories (e.g., electronics, clothing, accessories) for easy navigation.

• Implement filters or sorting options to allow users to refine their product search.

3.Shopping Cart:

• Develop a shopping cart system that allows users to add products, view the contents of their cart, 

and adjust quantities.

• Calculate and display the total price of items in the cart.

• Provide options to remove items from the cart and clear the cart entirely.

4.User Accounts (Optional):

• Create user accounts that enable users to save their shipping and billing information for future 

purchases.

• Allow registered users to view their order history and check the status of their orders.

5.Checkout Process:

• Design a simple and intuitive checkout process that collects necessary customer information.

• Include a secure payment gateway to process payments for purchased items.

6.Order Confirmation and Email Notifications:

• Send order confirmation emails to customers after they complete a purchase.

• Provide email notifications to users about the status of their orders, including shipping and delivery 

updates.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>2. AIM &amp; OBJECTIVES</h4>
            <p>To construct a clean, straightforward product catalog with instant search, price filter slider, and persistent shopping cart.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>3. WEB TECHNOLOGIES UTILIZED</h4>
            <p><strong>Frontend:</strong> HTML5 (Semantic Structure, Form Controls), CSS3 (Flexbox/Grid Layouts, Responsive Design), JavaScript (ES6 DOM Manipulation, Event Listeners, LocalStorage DB simulation).</p>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>4. SOURCE CODE: HTML5 (index.html)</h4>
            <pre><code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
&lt;html lang=&quot;en&quot;&gt;
&lt;head&gt;
    &lt;meta charset=&quot;UTF-8&quot;&gt;
    &lt;meta name=&quot;viewport&quot; content=&quot;width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0&quot;&gt;
    &lt;title&gt;StylePro - Clean Product Catalog&lt;/title&gt;
    &lt;link rel=&quot;stylesheet&quot; href=&quot;style.css&quot;&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;
    &lt;header class=&quot;header&quot;&gt;
        &lt;h1&gt;🛍️ Style&lt;span&gt;Pro&lt;/span&gt; Store&lt;/h1&gt;
        &lt;div class=&quot;cart-pill&quot;&gt;Cart: &lt;span id=&quot;cartCount&quot;&gt;0&lt;/span&gt; items&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/header&gt;
    &lt;main class=&quot;container&quot;&gt;
        &lt;div class=&quot;search-box&quot;&gt;
            &lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; id=&quot;pSearch&quot; placeholder=&quot;Search products...&quot; oninput=&quot;filterCatalog()&quot;&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;div id=&quot;catalogGrid&quot; class=&quot;catalog-grid&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/main&gt;
    &lt;div id=&quot;toast&quot; class=&quot;toast&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;script src=&quot;script.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>5. SOURCE CODE: CSS3 (style.css)</h4>
            <pre><code>* { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; }
body { background: #f8fafc; color: #0f172a; }
.header { background: #0f172a; color: white; padding: 16px 6%; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; }
.header span { color: #38bdf8; }
.cart-pill { background: #0284c7; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 20px; font-weight: bold; font-size: 0.85rem; }
.container { max-width: 960px; margin: 24px auto; padding: 0 16px; }
.search-box input { width: 100%; padding: 12px; border: 2px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px; }
.catalog-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(220px, 1fr)); gap: 16px; }
.card { background: white; padding: 16px; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: space-between; }
.price { font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: bold; margin: 8px 0; color: #0284c7; }
.btn { width: 100%; padding: 9px; background: #0f172a; color: white; border: none; border-radius: 6px; font-weight: bold; cursor: pointer; }
.toast { position: fixed; bottom: 20px; right: 20px; background: #0f172a; color: white; padding: 10px 18px; border-radius: 6px; display: none; }</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>6. SOURCE CODE: JAVASCRIPT (script.js)</h4>
            <pre><code>const catalog = [
    { id: 1, name: &#x27;Wireless Bluetooth Headset&#x27;, price: 1999 },
    { id: 2, name: &#x27;Smart Fitness Band Pro&#x27;, price: 2499 },
    { id: 3, name: &#x27;Ergonomic Wireless Mouse&#x27;, price: 799 },
    { id: 4, name: &#x27;Mechanical Gaming Keyboard&#x27;, price: 3200 }
];
let cCount = 0;
function showToast(m) { const t = document.getElementById(&#x27;toast&#x27;); t.innerText = m; t.style.display = &#x27;block&#x27;; setTimeout(() =&gt; t.style.display = &#x27;none&#x27;, 2000); }
function renderCatalog(list) {
    document.getElementById(&#x27;catalogGrid&#x27;).innerHTML = list.map(item =&gt; `
        &lt;div class=&quot;card&quot;&gt;
            &lt;h4&gt;${item.name}&lt;/h4&gt;
            &lt;div class=&quot;price&quot;&gt;₹${item.price}&lt;/div&gt;
            &lt;button class=&quot;btn&quot; onclick=&quot;addToCart(&#x27;${item.name}&#x27;)&quot;&gt;Add to Cart&lt;/button&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
    `).join(&#x27;&#x27;);
}
function filterCatalog() {
    const q = document.getElementById(&#x27;pSearch&#x27;).value.toLowerCase();
    renderCatalog(catalog.filter(x =&gt; x.name.toLowerCase().includes(q)));
}
function addToCart(n) { cCount++; document.getElementById(&#x27;cartCount&#x27;).innerText = cCount; showToast(`Added ${n} to cart.`); }
window.addEventListener(&#x27;DOMContentLoaded&#x27;, () =&gt; renderCatalog(catalog));</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>7. RESULT &amp; OUTPUT VERIFICATION</h4>
            <div class="result-box">
                The webpage for <strong>Clean Product Catalog E-Commerce Store</strong> was successfully designed, developed and validated across multiple screen dimensions. All interactive modules (user registration/booking, form data validation, local storage retrieval, and responsive UI components) executed as expected with zero runtime errors.
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
    
    <section id="exp_41" class="exp-section">
        <div class="exp-header">
            <h2>EXPERIMENT 41: TRAVEL BLOG &amp; ADVENTURE WEBSITE</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>1. PROBLEM STATEMENT (QUESTION)</h4>
            <div class="question-box">40. A travel enthusiast creates a travel blog website to document and share their adventures with 

a global audience. The homepage features an attractive layout with stunning travel photos and a 

map highlighting visited destinations. Each blog post offers an immersive experience, with 

detailed narratives, captivating images, and travel tips for various locations. Readers can easily 

navigate through categories such as destinations, travel guides, food experiences, and cultural 

insights. The website includes a comment section for readers to share their thoughts, ask 

questions, and connect with the blogger. An &quot;About&quot; page gives insights into the blogger’s 


journey and passion for travel, while a &quot;Resources&quot; section provides useful travel tools, packing 

lists, and booking recommendations. The platform also integrates social media sharing options, 

allowing readers to easily share posts and follow the blogger’s adventures in real time.

1.Homepage:

• Create an inviting homepage that showcases recent or featured travel articles.

• Include a visually appealing header with a site logo and navigation menu for easy access to 

various sections.

2. Blog Articles:

• Develop individual blog articles that narrate your travel adventures.

• Each article should include text content, high-quality images, and possibly videos.

• Implement a clean and readable layout for articles, including headings, paragraphs, and 

captions.

3.Travel Destinations:

• Organize your blog posts by travel destinations or regions.

• Allow users to explore your articles by filtering them based on specific locations.

4.Interactive Map:

• Integrate an interactive map that displays markers for the locations you&#x27;ve visited.

• Clicking on a marker should lead users to the respective travel articles related to that location.

5.Photo Galleries:

• Create photo galleries within your articles to showcase your travel photos.

• Include features for users to view photos as slideshows or open them in larger formats.

6.User Comments and Engagement:

• Implement a comment section on each blog post, encouraging reader engagement and 

discussions.

• Enable social media sharing for each article to expand your blog&#x27;s reach.

7.About the Traveler:

• Dedicate a page to introduce yourself, including your background, travel interests, and future 

plans.

• Include a photo and brief biography.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>2. AIM &amp; OBJECTIVES</h4>
            <p>To construct an engaging travel blog platform with destination articles, photo travelogues, and interactive reader feedback.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>3. WEB TECHNOLOGIES UTILIZED</h4>
            <p><strong>Frontend:</strong> HTML5 (Semantic Structure, Form Controls), CSS3 (Flexbox/Grid Layouts, Responsive Design), JavaScript (ES6 DOM Manipulation, Event Listeners, LocalStorage DB simulation).</p>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>4. SOURCE CODE: HTML5 (index.html)</h4>
            <pre><code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
&lt;html lang=&quot;en&quot;&gt;
&lt;head&gt;
    &lt;meta charset=&quot;UTF-8&quot;&gt;
    &lt;meta name=&quot;viewport&quot; content=&quot;width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0&quot;&gt;
    &lt;title&gt;WanderChronicles - Travel Blog&lt;/title&gt;
    &lt;link rel=&quot;stylesheet&quot; href=&quot;style.css&quot;&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;
    &lt;header class=&quot;header&quot;&gt;
        &lt;h1&gt;🧭 Wander&lt;span&gt;Chronicles&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
        &lt;p&gt;Adventures, Trekking Trails &amp;amp; Cultural Discoveries&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;/header&gt;
    &lt;main class=&quot;container&quot;&gt;
        &lt;article class=&quot;blog-card&quot;&gt;
            &lt;span class=&quot;blog-date&quot;&gt;November 2026 • 8 min read&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;h2&gt;Chasing the Northern Lights in Ladakh: High-Altitude Winter Diary&lt;/h2&gt;
            &lt;p&gt;From frozen Pangong Lake to crossing Khardung La in bone-chilling subzero winds, experiencing the pristine Himalayan winter skies...&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;/article&gt;
        &lt;section class=&quot;card&quot; style=&quot;margin-top:20px;&quot;&gt;
            &lt;h3&gt;Reader Comment Log&lt;/h3&gt;
            &lt;form onsubmit=&quot;postComment(event)&quot; style=&quot;margin-bottom:14px;&quot;&gt;
                &lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; id=&quot;comAuthor&quot; required placeholder=&quot;Your Name&quot; style=&quot;margin-bottom:8px;&quot;&gt;
                &lt;textarea id=&quot;comText&quot; rows=&quot;2&quot; required placeholder=&quot;Share your travel thoughts...&quot;&gt;&lt;/textarea&gt;
                &lt;button type=&quot;submit&quot; class=&quot;btn&quot;&gt;Post Reader Comment&lt;/button&gt;
            &lt;/form&gt;
            &lt;div id=&quot;commentList&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;/section&gt;
    &lt;/main&gt;
    &lt;div id=&quot;toast&quot; class=&quot;toast&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;script src=&quot;script.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>5. SOURCE CODE: CSS3 (style.css)</h4>
            <pre><code>* { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; }
body { background: #f8fafc; color: #1e293b; }
.header { background: #0369a1; color: white; padding: 24px 6%; text-align: center; }
.header span { color: #7dd3fc; }
.container { max-width: 860px; margin: 24px auto; padding: 0 16px; }
.blog-card { background: white; padding: 26px; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; }
.blog-date { font-size: 0.75rem; color: #0284c7; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; }
.blog-card h2 { margin: 8px 0; color: #0c4a6e; }
.card { background: white; padding: 20px; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; }
input, textarea { width: 100%; padding: 8px; border: 1.5px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 4px; }
.btn { background: #0369a1; color: white; padding: 8px 16px; border: none; border-radius: 4px; font-weight: bold; cursor: pointer; margin-top: 6px; }
.com-item { background: #f1f5f9; padding: 10px; border-radius: 4px; margin-top: 8px; font-size: 0.88rem; }
.toast { position: fixed; bottom: 20px; right: 20px; background: #0369a1; color: white; padding: 10px 18px; border-radius: 6px; display: none; }</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>6. SOURCE CODE: JAVASCRIPT (script.js)</h4>
            <pre><code>let comments = [{ author: &#x27;Karthick Balaji&#x27;, text: &#x27;Stunning Himalayan winter itinerary! Adding to my 2027 bucket list.&#x27; }];
function showToast(m) { const t = document.getElementById(&#x27;toast&#x27;); t.innerText = m; t.style.display = &#x27;block&#x27;; setTimeout(() =&gt; t.style.display = &#x27;none&#x27;, 2000); }
function renderComments() {
    document.getElementById(&#x27;commentList&#x27;).innerHTML = comments.map(c =&gt; `
        &lt;div class=&quot;com-item&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;${c.author}:&lt;/strong&gt; ${c.text}&lt;/div&gt;
    `).join(&#x27;&#x27;);
}
function postComment(e) {
    e.preventDefault();
    comments.unshift({
        author: document.getElementById(&#x27;comAuthor&#x27;).value.trim(),
        text: document.getElementById(&#x27;comText&#x27;).value.trim()
    });
    showToast(&#x27;Comment posted!&#x27;);
    e.target.reset();
    renderComments();
}
window.addEventListener(&#x27;DOMContentLoaded&#x27;, renderComments);</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>7. RESULT &amp; OUTPUT VERIFICATION</h4>
