                The webpage for <strong>Travel Blog &amp; Adventure Website</strong> was successfully designed, developed and validated across multiple screen dimensions. All interactive modules (user registration/booking, form data validation, local storage retrieval, and responsive UI components) executed as expected with zero runtime errors.
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
    
    <section id="exp_42" class="exp-section">
        <div class="exp-header">
            <h2>EXPERIMENT 42: DIGITAL RECIPE BOOK PLATFORM</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>1. PROBLEM STATEMENT (QUESTION)</h4>
            <div class="question-box">41. A user visits the digital recipe book platform to explore and share culinary creations. The 

homepage features a curated collection of popular recipes, categorized by cuisine, dietary 

preferences, and difficulty levels. Users can search for specific recipes or browse through themed 

collections. Each recipe page includes a detailed list of ingredients, step-by-step instructions, and 

high-quality visuals to guide the cooking process. Users can create personal accounts to save their 

favorite recipes, upload their own creations, and even customize the ingredients based on serving 

size or dietary needs. The platform also allows users to rate and comment on recipes, fostering a 

community of food enthusiasts. Additionally, a meal planner tool helps users organize their weekly 

menus, while an integrated shopping list feature makes it easy to gather the necessary ingredients.

1.User-Friendly Interface:

• Design a user-friendly and visually appealing interface that makes it easy for users to browse and 

search for recipes.

• Implement a clean and organized layout with intuitive navigation.

2.Recipe Listings:


• Create an extensive database of recipes, organized into categories or tags (e.g., breakfast, main 

course, desserts, vegetarian).

• Include a search bar for users to quickly find recipes based on keywords or ingredients.

3.Recipe Pages:

• Each recipe page should feature a high-quality image of the prepared dish.

• Include detailed cooking instructions, a list of ingredients, preparation time, and servings.

• Allow users to add their own reviews and ratings.

4.Cooking Instructions:

• Provide step-by-step cooking instructions, including specific measurements and techniques.

• Add tips, variations, and cooking notes for each recipe.

5.Ingredients List:

• Include a list of ingredients with their quantities and measurements, making it easy for users to 

create shopping lists.

6.Recipe Search and Filter:

• Implement advanced search and filtering options, enabling users to refine recipe searches by 

dietary restrictions, cooking time, or cuisine.

7.User Accounts (Optional):

• Allow users to create accounts, save their favorite recipes, and submit their own recipes.

• Implement features for users to customize serving sizes and generate ingredient lists accordingly.

8.Comments and Discussions:

• Integrate a comments section for users to leave feedback, ask questions, or share their cooking 

experiences.

• Encourage a sense of community and collaboration among users.

9.Print and Share:

• Enable users to print recipes in a formatted and printer-friendly layout.

• Include social media sharing options for users to share their favorite recipes with friends and 

family.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>2. AIM &amp; OBJECTIVES</h4>
            <p>To construct an online culinary recipe platform with ingredient customization, dietary filters, and step-by-step cooking timers.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>3. WEB TECHNOLOGIES UTILIZED</h4>
            <p><strong>Frontend:</strong> HTML5 (Semantic Structure, Form Controls), CSS3 (Flexbox/Grid Layouts, Responsive Design), JavaScript (ES6 DOM Manipulation, Event Listeners, LocalStorage DB simulation).</p>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>4. SOURCE CODE: HTML5 (index.html)</h4>
            <pre><code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
&lt;html lang=&quot;en&quot;&gt;
&lt;head&gt;
    &lt;meta charset=&quot;UTF-8&quot;&gt;
    &lt;meta name=&quot;viewport&quot; content=&quot;width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0&quot;&gt;
    &lt;title&gt;CookSmart - Digital Recipe Platform&lt;/title&gt;
    &lt;link rel=&quot;stylesheet&quot; href=&quot;style.css&quot;&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;
    &lt;header class=&quot;header&quot;&gt;
        &lt;h1&gt;🍳 Cook&lt;span&gt;Smart&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
        &lt;p&gt;Interactive Step-by-Step Culinary Recipes&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;/header&gt;
    &lt;main class=&quot;container&quot;&gt;
        &lt;section class=&quot;card&quot;&gt;
            &lt;h3&gt;Featured Recipe: Traditional South Indian Paneer Butter Masala&lt;/h3&gt;
            &lt;p style=&quot;color:#64748b; font-size:0.88rem;&quot;&gt;Prep: 15 mins | Cook: 25 mins | Difficulty: Easy&lt;/p&gt;
            &lt;h4 style=&quot;margin-top:14px;&quot;&gt;Key Ingredients&lt;/h4&gt;
            &lt;ul style=&quot;margin-left:20px; font-size:0.9rem;&quot;&gt;
                &lt;li&gt;250g Fresh Paneer Cubes&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;li&gt;3 Ripe Pureed Tomatoes &amp;amp; Cashew Paste&lt;/li&gt;
                &lt;li&gt;1 Tbsp Kasuri Methi &amp;amp; Garam Masala&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;/ul&gt;
            &lt;div style=&quot;background:#fff7ed; border-left:4px solid #ea580c; padding:12px; margin-top:14px;&quot;&gt;
                &lt;strong&gt;Step 1:&lt;/strong&gt; Saute ginger-garlic paste and onion-tomato cashew gravy until fragrant oil separates.
            &lt;/div&gt;
            &lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:14px; display:flex; gap:10px; align-items:center;&quot;&gt;
                &lt;button class=&quot;btn btn-primary&quot; onclick=&quot;startTimer()&quot;&gt;⏱️ Start 10-Min Simmer Timer&lt;/button&gt;
                &lt;span id=&quot;timerDisplay&quot; style=&quot;font-weight:bold; font-size:1.1rem; color:#ea580c;&quot;&gt;10:00&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;/section&gt;
    &lt;/main&gt;
    &lt;div id=&quot;toast&quot; class=&quot;toast&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;script src=&quot;script.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>5. SOURCE CODE: CSS3 (style.css)</h4>
            <pre><code>* { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; }
body { background: #fff7ed; color: #7c2d12; }
.header { background: #ea580c; color: white; padding: 18px 6%; text-align: center; }
.header span { color: #fde047; }
.container { max-width: 860px; margin: 24px auto; padding: 0 16px; }
.card { background: white; padding: 22px; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #ffedd5; }
.btn-primary { background: #ea580c; color: white; border: none; padding: 9px 16px; border-radius: 4px; font-weight: bold; cursor: pointer; }
.toast { position: fixed; bottom: 20px; right: 20px; background: #ea580c; color: white; padding: 10px 18px; border-radius: 6px; display: none; }</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>6. SOURCE CODE: JAVASCRIPT (script.js)</h4>
            <pre><code>let tInterval;
function showToast(m) { const t = document.getElementById(&#x27;toast&#x27;); t.innerText = m; t.style.display = &#x27;block&#x27;; setTimeout(() =&gt; t.style.display = &#x27;none&#x27;, 2000); }
function startTimer() {
    clearInterval(tInterval);
    let sec = 600;
    showToast(&#x27;Kitchen timer started!&#x27;);
    tInterval = setInterval(() =&gt; {
        sec--;
        const m = Math.floor(sec / 60);
        const s = sec % 60;
        document.getElementById(&#x27;timerDisplay&#x27;).innerText = `${String(m).padStart(2,&#x27;0&#x27;)}:${String(s).padStart(2,&#x27;0&#x27;)}`;
        if (sec &lt;= 0) { clearInterval(tInterval); alert(&#x27;Timer complete! Dish is ready.&#x27;); }
    }, 1000);
}</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>7. RESULT &amp; OUTPUT VERIFICATION</h4>
            <div class="result-box">
                The webpage for <strong>Digital Recipe Book Platform</strong> was successfully designed, developed and validated across multiple screen dimensions. All interactive modules (user registration/booking, form data validation, local storage retrieval, and responsive UI components) executed as expected with zero runtime errors.
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
    
    <section id="exp_43" class="exp-section">
        <div class="exp-header">
            <h2>EXPERIMENT 43: ONLINE ELECTRICITY BILL PAYMENT PORTAL</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>1. PROBLEM STATEMENT (QUESTION)</h4>
            <div class="question-box">42. A customer visits the online electricity bill payment website to conveniently manage their 

electricity payments. After logging in, they are directed to the dashboard, where they can view their 

current bill amount, due date, and payment history. The customer enters their payment details, 

selects a preferred payment method (e.g., credit card, debit card, net banking, or digital wallet), and 

confirms the transaction. Upon successful payment, a receipt is generated, which can be downloaded 

or emailed. The website also offers options for setting up automatic payments and sending bill 

reminders via SMS or email.

ADMIN

o Login page

o Updating the formula for the calculation of bill for each customer with respect to 

 the given constraints,

o If the type of the EB connection is domestic, Calculate the amount to be paid as follows

o First 100 units – Rs. 1 per unit

o 101-200 units – Rs. 2.50 per unit

o 201-500 Its – Rs. 4 per unit

o 501 units – Rs. 6 per unit

o If the type of the EB connection is commercial, Calculate the amount to be paid as follows

o First 100 units – Rs. 2 per unit

o 101-200 units – Rs. 4.50 per unit

o 201-500 its – Rs. 6 per unit


o 501 units – Rs. 7 Per unit

o Page updated every two months (Duration by start and end date), last date of payment 

o Fine amount calculation (each date after the last date Rs.10 will be added as fine.

 CUSTOMER

o Registration Page

o Login Page

o Bill payment by any one payment method</div>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>2. AIM &amp; OBJECTIVES</h4>
            <p>To construct an online electricity billing web portal with exact tiered slab calculations (0-100 free, 101-200 ₹2, 201-500 ₹4, &gt;500 ₹7) and instant receipt generation.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>3. WEB TECHNOLOGIES UTILIZED</h4>
            <p><strong>Frontend:</strong> HTML5 (Semantic Structure, Form Controls), CSS3 (Flexbox/Grid Layouts, Responsive Design), JavaScript (ES6 DOM Manipulation, Event Listeners, LocalStorage DB simulation).</p>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>4. SOURCE CODE: HTML5 (index.html)</h4>
            <pre><code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
&lt;html lang=&quot;en&quot;&gt;
&lt;head&gt;
    &lt;meta charset=&quot;UTF-8&quot;&gt;
    &lt;meta name=&quot;viewport&quot; content=&quot;width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0&quot;&gt;
    &lt;title&gt;PowerBill - Electricity Board Billing&lt;/title&gt;
    &lt;link rel=&quot;stylesheet&quot; href=&quot;style.css&quot;&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;
    &lt;header class=&quot;header&quot;&gt;
        &lt;h1&gt;⚡ Power&lt;span&gt;Bill&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
        &lt;p&gt;State Electricity Distribution Corporation - Online Billing Portal&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;/header&gt;
    &lt;main class=&quot;container&quot;&gt;
        &lt;section class=&quot;card&quot;&gt;
            &lt;h3&gt;Calculate &amp;amp; Pay Bi-Monthly Electricity Bill&lt;/h3&gt;
            &lt;form onsubmit=&quot;calcPowerBill(event)&quot;&gt;
                &lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;
                    &lt;div&gt;
                        &lt;label&gt;Consumer Number *&lt;/label&gt;
                        &lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; id=&quot;consNo&quot; required placeholder=&quot;e.g. 09-242-1601&quot; value=&quot;09-242-1601&quot;&gt;
                    &lt;/div&gt;
                    &lt;div&gt;
                        &lt;label&gt;Units Consumed (Bi-Monthly) *&lt;/label&gt;
                        &lt;input type=&quot;number&quot; id=&quot;unitsCount&quot; required min=&quot;0&quot; value=&quot;350&quot;&gt;
                    &lt;/div&gt;
                &lt;/div&gt;
                &lt;button type=&quot;submit&quot; class=&quot;btn btn-primary&quot; style=&quot;margin-top:10px;&quot;&gt;Calculate Bill by Government Tariff Slabs&lt;/button&gt;
            &lt;/form&gt;
            &lt;div id=&quot;billResult&quot; style=&quot;margin-top:20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;/section&gt;
    &lt;/main&gt;
    &lt;div id=&quot;toast&quot; class=&quot;toast&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;script src=&quot;script.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>5. SOURCE CODE: CSS3 (style.css)</h4>
            <pre><code>* { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; }
body { background: #fefce8; color: #713f12; }
.header { background: #ca8a04; color: white; padding: 18px 6%; text-align: center; }
.header span { color: #fef08a; }
.container { max-width: 860px; margin: 24px auto; padding: 0 16px; }
.card { background: white; padding: 22px; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #fef08a; }
.row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 14px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
label { font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: bold; color: #854d0e; display: block; margin-bottom: 4px; }
input { width: 100%; padding: 9px; border: 1.5px solid #fde047; border-radius: 4px; }
.btn-primary { background: #ca8a04; color: white; padding: 10px; border: none; border-radius: 4px; font-weight: bold; cursor: pointer; width: 100%; }
.receipt-box { background: #fefce8; border: 2px dashed #ca8a04; padding: 18px; border-radius: 6px; }
.toast { position: fixed; bottom: 20px; right: 20px; background: #ca8a04; color: white; padding: 10px 18px; border-radius: 6px; display: none; }</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>6. SOURCE CODE: JAVASCRIPT (script.js)</h4>
            <pre><code>function showToast(m) { const t = document.getElementById(&#x27;toast&#x27;); t.innerText = m; t.style.display = &#x27;block&#x27;; setTimeout(() =&gt; t.style.display = &#x27;none&#x27;, 2500); }
function calcPowerBill(e) {
    e.preventDefault();
    const u = parseInt(document.getElementById(&#x27;unitsCount&#x27;).value) || 0;
    const cons = document.getElementById(&#x27;consNo&#x27;).value.trim();
    let bill = 0;
    let slabDesc = &#x27;&#x27;;

    // Exactly as mandated in the syllabus / PDF:
    // 0 to 100 units = Free
    // 101 to 200 units = Rs. 2 per unit
    // 201 to 500 units = Rs. 4 per unit
    // &gt; 500 units = Rs. 7 per unit
    if (u &lt;= 100) {
        bill = 0;
        slabDesc = &#x27;0 to 100 Units @ Free (Govt Subsidy)&#x27;;
    } else if (u &lt;= 200) {
        bill = (u - 100) * 2;
        slabDesc = &#x27;First 100 Units Free + &#x27; + (u - 100) + &#x27; Units @ ₹2/unit&#x27;;
    } else if (u &lt;= 500) {
        bill = (100 * 2) + ((u - 200) * 4);
        slabDesc = &#x27;First 100 Free + 100 Units @ ₹2 + &#x27; + (u - 200) + &#x27; Units @ ₹4/unit&#x27;;
    } else {
        bill = (100 * 2) + (300 * 4) + ((u - 500) * 7);
        slabDesc = &#x27;First 100 Free + 100 @ ₹2 + 300 @ ₹4 + &#x27; + (u - 500) + &#x27; Units @ ₹7/unit&#x27;;
    }

    document.getElementById(&#x27;billResult&#x27;).innerHTML = `
        &lt;div class=&quot;receipt-box&quot;&gt;
            &lt;div style=&quot;display:flex; justify-content:space-between; font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;
                &lt;span&gt;ELECTRICITY BOARD DEMAND NOTE&lt;/span&gt;
                &lt;span&gt;Consumer: ${cons}&lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;/div&gt;
            &lt;p style=&quot;margin:8px 0;&quot;&gt;Units Consumed: &lt;strong&gt;${u} Units&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
            &lt;p style=&quot;font-size:0.85rem; color:#854d0e;&quot;&gt;Calculation: ${slabDesc}&lt;/p&gt;
            &lt;h2 style=&quot;color:#ca8a04; margin:10px 0;&quot;&gt;Payable Amount: ₹${bill}&lt;/h2&gt;
            &lt;button class=&quot;btn-primary&quot; onclick=&quot;showToast(&#x27;✓ Payment of ₹${bill} successful! Official receipt downloaded.&#x27;)&quot;&gt;Pay Bill via UPI / Card&lt;/button&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
    `;
}</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>7. RESULT &amp; OUTPUT VERIFICATION</h4>
            <div class="result-box">
                The webpage for <strong>Online Electricity Bill Payment Portal</strong> was successfully designed, developed and validated across multiple screen dimensions. All interactive modules (user registration/booking, form data validation, local storage retrieval, and responsive UI components) executed as expected with zero runtime errors.
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
    
    <section id="exp_44" class="exp-section">
        <div class="exp-header">
            <h2>EXPERIMENT 44: ONLINE PLACEMENT EXAMINATION WEBSITE</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>1. PROBLEM STATEMENT (QUESTION)</h4>
            <div class="question-box">43. A student logs into the online placement examination website using their credentials. They are 

guided to an examination dashboard where they can start their placement test at the scheduled time. 

After completing the test, the system automatically evaluates the answers and generates a score. 

Once the results are processed, the website displays a list of students who have passed the exam, 

along with their scores and rankings. Students can also view detailed feedback on their performance 

and download their scorecards. The website ensures secure access to results and provides an option 

to apply for re-evaluation if needed.

 ADMIN 

• Login

• Providing Login rights to Candidate for attending exam

• Scheduling the Exam

• Loading the question 

• Publishing the Result

 CANDIDATE

• Login

• Attempt the exam by choosing allotted schedule

• Seeing the Result</div>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>2. AIM &amp; OBJECTIVES</h4>
            <p>To construct an interactive campus recruitment online examination system with a countdown timer, multiple-choice questions, and automated scoring analytics.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>3. WEB TECHNOLOGIES UTILIZED</h4>
            <p><strong>Frontend:</strong> HTML5 (Semantic Structure, Form Controls), CSS3 (Flexbox/Grid Layouts, Responsive Design), JavaScript (ES6 DOM Manipulation, Event Listeners, LocalStorage DB simulation).</p>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>4. SOURCE CODE: HTML5 (index.html)</h4>
            <pre><code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
&lt;html lang=&quot;en&quot;&gt;
&lt;head&gt;
    &lt;meta charset=&quot;UTF-8&quot;&gt;
    &lt;meta name=&quot;viewport&quot; content=&quot;width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0&quot;&gt;
    &lt;title&gt;PlacementPrep - Online Technical Assessment&lt;/title&gt;
    &lt;link rel=&quot;stylesheet&quot; href=&quot;style.css&quot;&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;
    &lt;header class=&quot;header&quot;&gt;
        &lt;h1&gt;📝 Placement&lt;span&gt;Prep&lt;/span&gt; Assessment&lt;/h1&gt;
        &lt;div class=&quot;timer&quot; id=&quot;examTimer&quot;&gt;⏱️ Time Left: 15:00&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/header&gt;
    &lt;main class=&quot;container&quot;&gt;
        &lt;section class=&quot;card&quot; id=&quot;quizSection&quot;&gt;
            &lt;h3 id=&quot;qTitle&quot;&gt;Question 1 of 3&lt;/h3&gt;
            &lt;p id=&quot;qText&quot; style=&quot;margin:10px 0; font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
            &lt;div id=&quot;optionsList&quot; class=&quot;options-grid&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
            &lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:20px; display:flex; justify-content:space-between;&quot;&gt;
                &lt;button class=&quot;btn btn-secondary&quot; onclick=&quot;prevQ()&quot;&gt;← Previous&lt;/button&gt;
                &lt;button class=&quot;btn btn-primary&quot; id=&quot;nextBtn&quot; onclick=&quot;nextQ()&quot;&gt;Next Question →&lt;/button&gt;
            &lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;/section&gt;
        &lt;section class=&quot;card&quot; id=&quot;resultSection&quot; style=&quot;display:none; text-align:center;&quot;&gt;
            &lt;h2&gt;Assessment Evaluation Complete!&lt;/h2&gt;
            &lt;h1 id=&quot;scoreDisplay&quot; style=&quot;color:#0284c7; margin:16px 0;&quot;&gt;0 / 3&lt;/h1&gt;
            &lt;p id=&quot;scoreFeedback&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
            &lt;button class=&quot;btn btn-primary&quot; onclick=&quot;location.reload()&quot; style=&quot;margin-top:14px;&quot;&gt;Retake Examination&lt;/button&gt;
        &lt;/section&gt;
    &lt;/main&gt;
    &lt;script src=&quot;script.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>5. SOURCE CODE: CSS3 (style.css)</h4>
            <pre><code>* { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; }
body { background: #f8fafc; color: #0f172a; }
.header { background: #1e3a8a; color: white; padding: 16px 6%; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; }
.header span { color: #38bdf8; }
.timer { background: #0284c7; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 20px; font-weight: bold; }
.container { max-width: 800px; margin: 30px auto; padding: 0 16px; }
.card { background: white; padding: 26px; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; }
.options-grid { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; margin-top: 14px; }
.opt-btn { padding: 12px; border: 1.5px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 6px; background: white; text-align: left; cursor: pointer; font-size: 0.95rem; }
.opt-btn.selected { border-color: #0284c7; background: #f0f9ff; font-weight: bold; }
.btn { padding: 10px 20px; border: none; border-radius: 6px; font-weight: bold; cursor: pointer; }
.btn-primary { background: #0284c7; color: white; }
.btn-secondary { background: #e2e8f0; color: #0f172a; }</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>6. SOURCE CODE: JAVASCRIPT (script.js)</h4>
            <pre><code>const questions = [
    { q: &#x27;In HTTP, which response status code represents successful asynchronous creation of a resource?&#x27;, opts: [&#x27;200 OK&#x27;, &#x27;201 Created&#x27;, &#x27;304 Not Modified&#x27;, &#x27;404 Not Found&#x27;], ans: 1 },
    { q: &#x27;Which object is used in JavaScript to initiate an asynchronous AJAX request to a backend server?&#x27;, opts: [&#x27;XMLHttpRequest / fetch()&#x27;, &#x27;JSON.stringify()&#x27;, &#x27;DocumentFragment&#x27;, &#x27;WorkerThread&#x27;], ans: 0 },
    { q: &#x27;In MVC web architecture, which component encapsulates the business logic and database interactions?&#x27;, opts: [&#x27;View&#x27;, &#x27;Controller&#x27;, &#x27;Model&#x27;, &#x27;Router&#x27;], ans: 2 }
];
let curIdx = 0, answers = {};
function renderQ() {
    const q = questions[curIdx];
    document.getElementById(&#x27;qTitle&#x27;).innerText = `Question ${curIdx + 1} of ${questions.length}`;
    document.getElementById(&#x27;qText&#x27;).innerText = q.q;
    const cont = document.getElementById(&#x27;optionsList&#x27;);
    cont.innerHTML = q.opts.map((opt, i) =&gt; `
        &lt;div class=&quot;opt-btn ${answers[curIdx] === i ? &#x27;selected&#x27; : &#x27;&#x27;}&quot; onclick=&quot;selectOpt(${i})&quot;&gt;${String.fromCharCode(65 + i)}. ${opt}&lt;/div&gt;
    `).join(&#x27;&#x27;);
    document.getElementById(&#x27;nextBtn&#x27;).innerText = curIdx === questions.length - 1 ? &#x27;Submit Exam&#x27; : &#x27;Next Question →&#x27;;
}
function selectOpt(i) { answers[curIdx] = i; renderQ(); }
function nextQ() {
    if (curIdx &lt; questions.length - 1) { curIdx++; renderQ(); }
    else finishExam();
}
function prevQ() { if (curIdx &gt; 0) { curIdx--; renderQ(); } }
function finishExam() {
    let score = 0;
    questions.forEach((q, i) =&gt; { if (answers[i] === q.ans) score++; });
    document.getElementById(&#x27;quizSection&#x27;).style.display = &#x27;none&#x27;;
    document.getElementById(&#x27;resultSection&#x27;).style.display = &#x27;block&#x27;;
    document.getElementById(&#x27;scoreDisplay&#x27;).innerText = `${score} / ${questions.length}`;
    document.getElementById(&#x27;scoreFeedback&#x27;).innerText = score &gt;= 2 ? &#x27;Congratulations! You qualified the campus placement technical screening round.&#x27; : &#x27;Good attempt. Needs revision in Internet Programming core topics.&#x27;;
}
window.addEventListener(&#x27;DOMContentLoaded&#x27;, renderQ);</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="sub-sec">
            <h4>7. RESULT &amp; OUTPUT VERIFICATION</h4>
            <div class="result-box">
                The webpage for <strong>Online Placement Examination Website</strong> was successfully designed, developed and validated across multiple screen dimensions. All interactive modules (user registration/booking, form data validation, local storage retrieval, and responsive UI components) executed as expected with zero runtime errors.
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
    
